
                      Best of GEnie..... March 1988
  News from the GEnie Forth RoundTable by Gary Smith
    
   When I was asked to begin a 'Best of GEnie' column for 'Forth Dimensions'
I immediately realized I wanted Leonard Morgenstern's Topic area to be among
the first areas presented. Leonard has done a marvelous job of presenting our
language of choice in bite ( byte ? ) size chunks, and in such an entertaining
fashion as to create a novice and experienced Forth user tutorial area. 
   
   Time constraints and the shear depth of material available in Leonard's area
dictated making the entire first 'Best of GEnie' column an extraction of that
one Topic. Future installations will include discussions of the ANS FORTH X3/
J14 Technical Committee. Those of you who are not aware the future of Forth is
being decided on GEnie NOW are missing an opportunity to make your wishes known.
  
  Besides serving as the centerpiece in the first 'Best of GEnie' Leonard had
several coinciding events that make March 1988 especially memorable. He just
celebrated a birthday and his retirement from the rat race. He also graciously
accepted an offer to join Dennis Ruffer, Scott Squires and me as co-hosts of 
the Forth RoundTable on GEnie. Congratulations, Leonard, and 'Thank you'.

